# isopod per-agent colors — read by agent_preset().
#
# A session's bar takes the BOX's color by default, the way `isopod code` tints
# the IDE. These are what `--color agent` selects instead, which is how two
# agents running in the same box are told apart. The hex behind each preset name
# lives in share/colors; the colors are picked to be distinct from each other
# rather than to match anyone's brand.
#
# Override per agent with ISOPOD_<AGENT>_COLOR (a preset name, '#rrggbb', 'box'
# or 'agent'), or per run with --color. --no-color runs with no bar.
#
# agent     preset
claude      orange
codex       teal
opencode    blue
pi          purple
